    "description": "• Develop, maintain, and own production-critical software used in industrial manufacturing environments.\n\n• Rebuilt and modernized a legacy industrial monitoring platform using C#/.NET and WPF, scaling it from roughly 20 to 400+ concurrent machine connections.\n\n• Design and maintain SQL Server databases, reporting systems, REST APIs, integrations, and internal business applications.\n\n• Develop desktop and web applications using C#, .NET, WPF, ASP.NET, Entity Framework, LINQ, MVVM, and related technologies.\n\n• Diagnose complex production issues spanning application code, databases, networking, servers, hardware, and embedded systems.\n\n• Develop software integrations with industrial equipment and embedded hardware using TCP/IP and custom communication protocols.\n\n• Modernize legacy applications while maintaining compatibility with active production environments.\n\n• Manage Windows and Linux servers, deployments, backups, databases, and supporting IT infrastructure.\n\n• Work directly with enterprise customers on technical requirements, deployments, troubleshooting, and production support.\n\n• Own projects throughout the complete lifecycle—from requirements and architecture through development, deployment, troubleshooting, and long-term support.",
