    "description": "Special Olympics is the philanthropy of Phi Sigma Kappa. Special Olympics is an international program of year-round sports training and athletic competition for individuals with intellectual disabilities. Its goal is for all to have the chance to become useful and productive citizens who are accepted and respected in their communities. The benefits of participation in Special Olympics for individuals with intellectual disabilities include improved physical fitness and motor skills, greater self-confidence, a more positive self-image, friendships and increased family support. \n\nOn average, Phi Sigma Kappa raises $75,000 for Special Olympics each year, through fundraisers, sponsorships, and events held by our undergraduate brothers. \n\nAlso, Phi Sigma Kappa members serve 13,000 volunteer hours each year for Special Olympics.",
